    "entry_sha256": "ccd56936288b0cfe8b8d8532c79a0313e059c20a15fe559d815ff79d719afd63"
  },
  "rules": {
    "oracle": "Whenever this Vehicle attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature that crewed it this turn. Then if that creature is a Mutant, Ninja, or Turtle, double the number of +1/+1 counters on it.\nCrew 1 (Tap any number of creatures you control with total power 1 or more: This Vehicle becomes an artifact creature until end of turn.)",
    "cr": [
      "702.122a",
      "702.122c",
      "508.1m",
      "603.2",
      "608.2c",
      "122.6"
    ],
    "actual": "The coverage report lists the card as unsupported with one gap, `Swallow:Duration_ThisTurn` (\"Whenever this Vehicle attacks, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature that crewed it this turn. Then if that creature is a Mutant, Ninja, or…\"): it claims the parser dropped the clause's \"this turn\".",
    "expected": "Whenever Turtle Van attacks, its controller puts a +1/+1 counter on target creature that crewed it during this turn (CR 702.122c); then, if that creature is a Mutant, Ninja or Turtle, the number of +1/+1 counters on it is doubled (putting as many as it already has, per the card's ruling). A creature that crewed it on an earlier turn is not a legal target.",
    "diagnosis": "False positive. The \"this turn\" is part of the target filter `FilterProp::CrewedThisTurn { relation: CrewedSource }`, which reads `crew_history_this_turn` (types/game_state.rs:23170-23178; recorded when the crew cost is paid, cleared at turn start, game/turns.rs:1677). The Duration_ThisTurn detector (parser/swallow_check.rs:5367, `detect_duration_this_turn`) lists the turn-history `FilterProp` carriers it accepts (parser/swallow_check.rs:5668-5680), and `CrewedThisTurn` is not among them, although it is turn-scoped by construction; the suffix list has \"saddled it this turn\" (parser/swallow_check.rs:5476) but not \"crewed it this turn\". game/coverage.rs:8316 then turns the `SwallowedClause` into a `Swallow:Duration_ThisTurn` gap, which marks the card unsupported.",
    "suggested_fix": "Add `FilterProp::CrewedThisTurn { .. }` to the `FilterProp` arm of `detect_duration_this_turn` (parser/swallow_check.rs, next to `AttackedThisTurn`/`BlockedThisTurn`), or add \"crewed it this turn\" to `QUANTITY_CONTEXT_SUFFIXES` beside \"saddled it this turn\" (CR 702.122c is the crew counterpart of CR 702.171c). Regression test: Turtle Van parses with no `SwallowedClause` and stays supported in the coverage report.",
    "override_note": "Nothing is patched: the test ops pin what the sandbox games verified: the attack trigger, its target filter (a creature that crewed this Vehicle this turn), the doubling sub-ability on that same target gated on Mutant, Ninja or Turtle, and the Crew 1 keyword. The cases show a Turtle crewer getting two counters, a Ninja crewer (Karai) two, a Grizzly Bears crewer one, a Turtle that already had a counter going to four, a creature that crewed it two turns earlier not being a legal target (only this turn's crewer is), and with two crewers the condition reading the chosen target."
  },
